      <node id="EventNode:9d66207f-c495-436e-a83e-bb3c551206a8" label="Symptom | 2026-01-07 11:00:00 | Yuri Matsumoto (FY1)  Presenting Complaint 3-day hx of abdomin...">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="Clinical Event" />
          <attvalue for="1" value="Symptom" />
          <attvalue for="2" value="2026-01-07 11:00:00" />
          <attvalue for="3" value="Yuri Matsumoto (FY1)&#10;&#10;Presenting Complaint&#10;3-day hx of abdominal pain - 3-day hx of worsening adominal pain - Site: Lower abdmoen - Onset: Gradual - Character: Dull ache - Radiates: No radiartion - Associations: Constipation, reduced appetite - Timing: Constant - Exacerbating factors: Eating - Severity: 6/10 on arrival, reduced to 5/10 after IV fluids (0.9% sodium chloride) in ED - Note: Single dose of 10mg bisacodyl administered in ED&#10;&#10;Review of Systems&#10;- Cardiovascular: No chest pain, palpitations, or dizziness&#10;- Respiratory: No SOB or cough&#10;- Gastrointestinal: Abdominal pain as described, constipation, no nausea or vomiting, no melaena, no haematochezia&#10;- Genitourinary: No dysuria or haematuria&#10;- Neurological: No headaches, weakness, or altered coonsciousjess&#10;- Musculoskeletal: No joint or muscle pain&#10;- ENT: No sore throat or ear pain&#10;- Dermatological: No rashes or skin changes&#10;&#10;Past Medical History&#10;- Nil&#10;&#10;Medications&#10;- None&#10;&#10;Allergies&#10;No known drug allergies&#10;&#10;Social History&#10;- Lives with parents&#10;- Attends schol full-time&#10;- Independent in activities of daily living&#10;- No history of smoking, alcohol, or recreational drug use&#10;&#10;Family History&#10;No known familial history of gastrointestinal ior other relevant conditions&#10;&#10;On Examination&#10;- Alert, sitting comfortably, no acute distress&#10;- Abdominal examination:&#10;  - Inspection: Abdomen distenedd, no visible scars or masses&#10;  - Palpation: Mild tenderness in bilateral lower quad rants (BLQ), no guarding or rebound tenderness&#10;  - Percussion: Tympanic over large bowel&#10;  - Auscultation: Normakl bowel sounds (NBS)&#10;- Hydration assessment:&#10;  - Mildly dry mucous membranes (MM)&#10;  - Skin turgor slightly reduced&#10;- No other significant findings on systemic examination&#10;&#10;Observations&#10;HR 92&#10;BP 110/72&#10;RR 16&#10;Temp 36.8&#10;SpO2 99%&#10;&#10;Investigations&#10;- Abdominal X-ray: Significant faecal loaading noted, no evidence of obstruction or perforation&#10;- Blood tests: Normal FBC, U&amp;Es, and CRP&#10;- No other test results pending&#10;&#10;Impression&#10;Constipation with associated abdominal pain and mild dehydration&#10;&#10;Plan&#10;- Prescribe oral macrogol 13.8g sachets, 1 sachet TID as per ED recommendation&#10;- Encourage oral fluid intake to address dehydration&#10;- Monitor bowel movements andabdominal symptoms&#10;- Reassess hydration status and abdominal symptoms after 24 hours&#10;- If no significant improvement in symptoms after 24 hours, consider aditional imaging or alternative laxatives&#10;&#10;&#10;Dr." />
          <attvalue for="4" value="RECORDED" />
          <attvalue for="5" value="9d66207f-c495-436e-a83e-bb3c551206a8" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="88ed813c-7ca9-4fac-b57d-c2005a4bb8ba" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
